      "message": "+CC: @qwandor@google.com as well for Rust advise.\n\n\nI loved the idea but I couldn\u0027t make it work after spending couple of days.\n\n\nHere\u0027s my trial (doesn\u0027t compile).\n\n```\n    fn mask_internal(\u0026mut self, path: \u0026DtPathTokens, leaf_mask: DeviceTreeChildrenMask) -\u003e bool {\n        let mut path_token_iter \u003d path.tokens.iter().peekable();\n        let mut mask_iter \u003d self;\n\n        \u0027next_token: while let Some(path_token) \u003d path_token_iter.peek() {\n            let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n                // DeviceTreeChildrenMask::All. Everything is masked already.\n                return false;\n            };\n\n            for i in 0..children.len() {\n                if children[i].name_bytes.as_slice() \u003d\u003d **path_token {\n                    mask_iter \u003d \u0026mut children[i];\n                    path_token_iter.next();\n                    continue \u0027next_token;\n                }\n            }\n            break;\n        }\n\n        while let Some(path_token) \u003d path_token_iter.peek() {\n            let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n                panic!(\"Should not happen\");\n            };\n\n            let child \u003d Self {\n                name_bytes: path_token.to_vec(),\n                children: DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(Vec::new()),\n            };\n            children.push(child);\n            mask_iter \u003d children.last_mut().unwrap();\n\n            path_token_iter.next();\n        }\n\n        if leaf_mask \u003d\u003d DeviceTreeChildrenMask::All \u0026\u0026 mask_iter.children !\u003d leaf_mask {\n            mask_iter.children \u003d leaf_mask;\n            true\n        } else {\n            false\n        }\n    }\n\n```\n\nI don\u0027t know why, but Rust complaints that `mask_iter` is borrowed multiple times. (line number isn\u0027t accurate)\n\n```\nerror[E0499]: cannot borrow `mask_iter.children` as mutable more than once at a time\n   --\u003e packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/device_assignment.rs:268:69\n    |\n252 |             let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n    |                                                                     ----------------------- first mutable borrow occurs here\n...\n268 |             let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n    |                                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    |                                                                     |\n    |                                                                     second mutable borrow occurs here\n    |                                                                     first borrow later used here\n\nerror[E0502]: cannot borrow `mask_iter.children` as immutable because it is also borrowed as mutable\n   --\u003e packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/device_assignment.rs:282:56\n    |\n252 |             let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n    |                                                                     ----------------------- mutable borrow occurs here\n...\n282 |         if leaf_mask \u003d\u003d DeviceTreeChildrenMask::All \u0026\u0026 mask_iter.children !\u003d leaf_mask {\n    |                                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    |                                                        |\n    |                                                        immutable borrow occurs here\n    |                                                        mutable borrow later used here\n\nerror[E0506]: cannot assign to `mask_iter.children` because it is borrowed\n   --\u003e packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/device_assignment.rs:283:13\n    |\n252 |             let DeviceTreeChildrenMask::Partial(ref mut children) \u003d \u0026mut mask_iter.children else {\n    |                                                                     ----------------------- `mask_iter.children` is borrowed here\n...\n283 |             mask_iter.children \u003d leaf_mask;\n    |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    |             |\n    |             `mask_iter.children` is assigned to here but it was already borrowed\n    |             borrow later used here\n```\n\n\nDo you have any suggestion here? Otherwise I\u0027ll just keep current snippet because there\u0027s not much performance issue here.",
